      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T17:11:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general Skia already doesn\u0027t trust anything about what is in these typeless dictionaries. The change to `src/ports/SkTypeface_mac_ct.cpp` doesn\u0027t appear to be needed at all (I think the existing code is already correct). The change to `src/utils/mac/SkCTFont.cpp` is interesting as something should change here, but I\u0027m pretty sure it should be different logically. Will take a look into that.",
      "revId": "13dd292c42c94e37e46e5ab301ab7d9713fdaff1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd63797e_7e4ade50",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 19324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T17:24:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was unable to trace through what the callers were doing.\n\nIf indeed it is the case that any CFBooleanRef value would result in the code using the value 0, then I will abandon this CL as not needed.",
      "revId": "13dd292c42c94e37e46e5ab301ab7d9713fdaff1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75cce7a7_64f6cab3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 19324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T17:37:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note this is motivated, not by any error message from Skia, but from a font test that fails on Ventura, https://crbug.com/1372420, and I wanted to patch callers in this area.",
      "revId": "13dd292c42c94e37e46e5ab301ab7d9713fdaff1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "248ad33a_e7d70052",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T18:23:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pointing out this issue to us as yet another place we should make sure we aren\u0027t trusting the types in these dictionaries and doing something sane if they aren\u0027t as expected. I\u0027m pretty sure `find_dict_CGFloat` and how it is used with `SkCTFontDescriptorGetSkFontStyle` was done that way specifically because of similar issues in the past. However, it appears that `SkCTFontGetDataFontWeightMapping` should probably be tweaked. That one is less noticeable since the only effect is to report the weights of fonts created from data slightly different from correct, which generally doesn\u0027t show up in Chromium.",
      "parentUuid": "75cce7a7_64f6cab3",
      "revId": "13dd292c42c94e37e46e5ab301ab7d9713fdaff1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21fcd48e_7e231b3c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T18:23:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, in `src/ports/SkTypeface_mac_ct.cpp` we\u0027re doing exactly that. Mostly because we already don\u0027t trust what\u0027s in any of these dictionaries (half the code in this file is about not trusting what\u0027s in these dictionaries and what to do if they don\u0027t contain the expected types).\n\nHowever, `src/utils/mac/SkCTFont.cpp` probably should probably change behavior a bit to match. Created https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/590553 for that.",
      "parentUuid": "fd63797e_7e4ade50",
      "revId": "13dd292c42c94e37e46e5ab301ab7d9713fdaff1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff4a9b62_9b19444f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 19324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T18:30:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This sounds like correctness hardening, so that’s good news that this doesn’t need to be cherry-picked.",
      "parentUuid": "248ad33a_e7d70052",
      "revId": "13dd292c42c94e37e46e5ab301ab7d9713fdaff1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10c78ab9_13bc591b",
        "filename": "src/ports/SkTypeface_mac_ct.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 291,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T17:11:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A change like this would require renaming this method. On the other hand this is also not needed, since the callers already default to the value of 0 for other reasons like the referred issue.\n\nIn particular there is no need to drag any CFBoolean stuff into this, since the idea is to allow the user of this method to determine what to do on failure (and not try to magically interpret other things). In this case the one user (`SkCTFontDescriptorGetSkFontStyle`) already decided that if something unexpected is in here to set the values to 0.",
      "revId": "13dd292c42c94e37e46e5ab301ab7d9713fdaff1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68146632_534feda9",
        "filename": "src/utils/mac/SkCTFont.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 403,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T17:11:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here there is no need to bring anything about CFBoolean into the mix. More generically we shouldn\u0027t be trusting anything about what\u0027s in the dictionary and take any non-CFNumber to be 0, like `SkCTFontDescriptorGetSkFontStyle` already does.\n\nIndeed, the behavior here should almost match the existing behavior of `SkCTFontDescriptorGetSkFontStyle`. If the trait dict entry doesn\u0027t exist then we should return early (use the default). If the entry isn\u0027t a CFNumber then the weight should be 0. The test to bail early should be if the values aren\u0027t strictly monotonically increasing.",
      "revId": "13dd292c42c94e37e46e5ab301ab7d9713fdaff1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
